 "status": "urban",
 "summary": "The largest set of geometric earthworks known: an octagon joined to a circle, a 1200 ft great circle, a square and miles of parallel walls. Most of it now lies under the city of Newark. The Octagon and the Great Circle survive.",
 "notes": [
  "Only the Octagon with its attached circle and the Great Circle still stand; the plate's square, parallel walls and small circles lie under streets and houses.",
  "The overlay is rubber-sheeted: each surviving feature is fitted to its LiDAR walls on its own, because the plate's bearing from the Octagon to the Great Circle is about 7 degrees off.",
  "The Great Circle walls stand over a metre above the ground beside them, the highest of any site here."
